 "voiceover": "[excited, conversational] Wait — Anthropic's unreleased AI just built working hacks for Chrome, Safari, Windows and Linux. [serious] It happened in a lab, and every flaw was reported first. The worst is a Linux bug rated 9.8 out of 10. Anthropic's AI used it to get root control, no password needed. Ubuntu and Red Hat had no fix as of October 29.\n\n[amused] Meanwhile, Tokyo Electron's profit jumped 27% on AI chip demand. It makes chip-making equipment, and it announced a ¥150 billion buyback.\n\n[curious] And in Kentucky, university administrator David Durman won a religious exemption from using AI at work. He's a nontheistic humanist. [playful] No god required.\n\n[playful] And Zwift launched Zwift Plus, with an AI coach and real-road video. In the US, it's $29.99 a month, $10 more than standard.\n\n[confident] So AI is hacking, building chips, and coaching your workouts. If you run Linux servers, check your patches.\n\n[playful, warm] Send this to the friend who still says AI can't do real work.",
